    "Lighthouse ran DESKTOP only (formFactor=desktop, verified in the report configSettings). Mobile performance would typically score 10-20 points lower. These are not mobile-first scores.",
    "Schema.org: DataForSEO instant_pages returned has_micromarkup=false on all 6 URLs, but direct HTML inspection found parseable JSON-LD on every page (home: Organization/WebSite/LocalBusiness; services hub and contact: Organization/WebSite/LocalBusiness/FAQPage/BreadcrumbList; service landings: Service/LocalBusiness/FAQPage/BreadcrumbList; service area: LocalBusiness/FAQPage/BreadcrumbList). The DataForSEO flag is a false negative and is NOT treated as a missing-schema issue.",
    "TBT_ms is 0 on all 6 pages. INP_ms is null on all 6: lab Lighthouse does not emit interaction-to-next-paint. Both recorded as measured.",
    "Broken-link detection: on_page/instant_pages audits a single URL and does not crawl outlinks, so link-level 4xx/5xx checks were not performed. instant_pages reported broken_links=false and broken_resources=false on all 6 pages and every audited URL returned 200.",
    "Unweighted Lighthouse audits are excluded from lighthouse_issues. agent-accessibility-tree (agentic-browsing category, not scored) failed on all 6 URLs with the same root cause as link-name, which is recorded.",
    "DataForSEO no_image_title (images without a title attribute) fired on all 6 pages. It is not in the on-page rubric and has no SEO or accessibility impact when alt is present (alt coverage is 100% on all 6 pages), so it is not recorded as an issue, consistent with prior runs.",
    "Lab variance: LCP rose 67-326ms on 5 of 6 pages while performance scores moved only 0-1 points. Only /contact/ (+326ms) crossed the 200ms regression threshold; its LCP breakdown subparts sum to about 300ms, so the 1172ms figure is partly simulated throttling overhead. All 6 LCPs remain under 1.2s, well inside the 2.5s good threshold. Re-check next month before investing in a fix beyond the priority-hint change already recommended."
